Subject: [PATCH] drm: bridge: lt9611: initialize clock before publishing bridge

Apply after 0039 INSTEAD of diagnostic 0040/0041. The delayed crystal write
in build 694 still leaves the target unresponsive. Later full reset and
reinitialization restores transport with the crystal selected. Try bounded
hardware-reset recovery before enabling HPD IRQs or publishing the bridge.

Initialize clock/power at probe and retry once from hardware reset for a
clock transport failure. Restore revision/I2C initialization after every
reset. Preserve final errors, existing transfer retries and crystal values.
No reset/rebind from an active DRM callback, new sleep or boot-option change.

It is NOT established that immediate early reset reproduces successful late
recovery. This candidate still needs natural cold/warm startup validation;
source/mock tests and manual recovery are not boot acceptance. Remove the
ineffective one-second settling experiment rather than accumulating delays.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [unqualified DT510 startup recovery candidate]
Assisted-by: Briar
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/lontium-lt9611.c
@@ -1160,6 +1160,34 @@
+static int lt9611_boot_init(struct lt9611 *lt9611)
+{
+	int ret, attempt;
+
+	for (attempt = 0; attempt < 2; attempt++) {
+		lt9611_reset(lt9611);
+		lt9611->power_on = false;
+		lt9611->sleep = false;
+
+		ret = lt9611_read_device_rev(lt9611);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+
+		ret = lt9611_power_on(lt9611);
+		if (!ret)
+			return 0;
+		if (ret != -EAGAIN && ret != -ETIMEDOUT &&
+		    ret != -ENXIO)
+			return ret;
+
+		if (!attempt)
+			dev_warn(lt9611->dev,
+				 "clock/power init failed %d; resetting once\n", ret);
+	}
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
 static int lt9611_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 {
 	struct lt9611 *lt9611;
 	struct device *dev = &client->dev;
 	int ret;
 
@@ -1205,7 +1233,5 @@
-	lt9611_reset(lt9611);
-
-	ret = lt9611_read_device_rev(lt9611);
+	ret = lt9611_boot_init(lt9611);
 	if (ret) {
-		dev_err(dev, "failed to read chip rev\n");
+		dev_err(dev, "failed to initialize chip clock/power: %d\n", ret);
 		goto err_disable_regulators;
 	}
